<tr>
<td width= "800" valign="top" halign="center" style="padding-top: 25px" >

  <p style="text-align: justify; line-height: 1.6;">
    I am currently a Senior Research Fellow at the National University of Singapore, working with Prof. <a href="https://www.comp.nus.edu.sg/~dyhsu/">David Hsu</a>. In May 2026, I will join the Shanghai Innovation Institute as an Assistant Professor. Before joining NUS, I was a robotics researcher at ByteDance Research, working with <a href="https://www.taokong.org/">Tao Kong</a>. I finished my PhD in Control Science and Engineering at Xi'an Jiaotong University in 2022, advised by Prof. <a href="http://gr.xjtu.edu.cn/web/zeuslan">Xuguang Lan</a>.
  </p>

  <h3 style="margin-top: 30px; margin-bottom: 15px; text-align: left; font-weight: bold;">Research</h3>

  <p style="text-align: justify; line-height: 1.6;">
    My research studies <strong style="color: #CC0000; font-weight: bold;">structuring uncertainty for open-world manipulation</strong> that develops physically-grounded and reliable intelligence for long-horizon robotic tasks in open-world, dynamic environments. We build systems that actively treat uncertainty as a signal for decision-making. We systematically explore how to structure and utilize uncertainty across three primary domains:
  </p>
  <ul style="text-align: left; line-height: 1.6;">
    <li style="margin-bottom: 5px;"><strong style="font-weight: bold;">Uncertainty-aware task specification and planning</strong> that actively resolves language ambiguity via human-robot interaction and quantifies perception uncertainty for robust decision-making.</li>
    <li style="margin-bottom: 5px;"><strong style="font-weight: bold;">Object-centric scene representation for mobile manipulation</strong> that abstracts unstructured environments into scalable, hybrid symbolic-metric graphs to maintain consistent world beliefs under partial observability.</li>
    <li style="margin-bottom: 5px;"><strong style="font-weight: bold;">Composable and scalable manipulation skills</strong> that decompose low-level control into object-centric geometric primitives, enabling strong generalization and geometric feasibility via bi-level planning.</li>
  </ul>

  <p style="text-align: left; margin-top: 25px; line-height: 1.6;">
    <a href="#" style="color: #2053AB; text-decoration: none;">We are recruiting interns working on human-robot interaction and uncertainty-aware planning for robotics! Drop me an email if you are interested.</a>
  </p>

</td>
